NAME
    write - write 1, 2, or 4 bytes to a memory space

SYNOPSIS
    write <space> <addr> <value> [-w 1|2|4] [--le|--be] [--dec|--float] [--json]

DESCRIPTION
    Writes a 1-, 2-, or 4-byte value into writable memory space <space> at
    hex address <addr>. Defaults to 1-byte hexadecimal (or 4 bytes when
    --float is passed) and uses the space's native byte order unless --le
    or --be is specified. Refuses read-only memory spaces (see spaces(1)).

    For persistent per-frame writes or ROM-read intercepts, use cheat(1).
    For bulk writes from a file, use load(1).

EXAMPLES
    write WRAM 10 ff
    write RDRAM 100 999 -w 2 --be --dec --json

EXIT STATUS
    0   Value written (or usage/read-only refusal printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid argument, or session
        service fault.

SEE ALSO
    mem(1), load(1), dump(1), spaces(1), cheat(1)
